# Excluded from `helm package`, i.e. from the tarball a consumer installs.
#
# ci/ is why this file exists. It holds negative-tests.sh and its values fixtures, and they are
# CI-only: nothing under templates/ reads them (no .Files.Get touches ci/), and both workflows
# run the script from the source tree by path - charts/hephaisto/ci/negative-tests.sh - never
# from a package.
#
# Shipping them also shipped an assertion that CANNOT pass inside a package. negative-tests.sh
# asserts "Chart.yaml still reads 0.0.0", which is true of the git source and false of every
# published chart by construction, because `helm package --version` stamps the real number in.
# A consumer who ran the suite that came inside the tarball got 23/24 - a guard working
# correctly on the wrong subject, which is worse than no guard at all because it looks like a
# real failure.
ci/

# Version control and packaging noise.
.git/
.gitignore
*.tgz

# Editor and OS droppings.
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.bak
*.orig
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
